| Age 47","financial_summary":["Delek Logistics Partners, L.P. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.1B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","The company is burning through $31M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 59% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 39% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3872774107474904},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 62/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Delek Logistics Partners (DKL) Just Gave Investors Something To Think About","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-dkl/delek-logistics-partners/news/delek-logistics-partners-dkl-just-gave-investors-something-t","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794617149.075,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Delek Logistics Partners LP (DKL) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Guidance Raised as Sour ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/delek-logistics-partners-lp-dkl-030242794.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794366162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"(DKL) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/DKL_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_111026065602_1794354962.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794354962.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0